CAT = "s24Settlement"; SEG = "STL"
Q = [
('Under SEC Rule 10b-10, a broker-dealer must give the customer a written confirmation of a trade:',
 'At or before completion of the transaction', ['Within 10 business days after settlement', "With the customer's next monthly statement", 'Only if the customer asks for one in writing'],
 'Rule 10b-10(a) requires written notification at or before completion of the transaction, disclosing the capacity in which the firm acted and the other required details.'),
("A firm that is not a market maker in a listed stock fills a customer's purchase as riskless principal. Under Rule 10b-10 the confirmation must show:",
 "The reported trade price, the customer's price and the difference", ["The name of the other party to the firm's offsetting trade", "The representative's payout rate", "The firm's net capital that day"],
 'Rule 10b-10(a)(2)(ii)(A) requires a firm that is not a market maker and buys or sells an equity security to offset a contemporaneous customer trade to disclose, for a last-sale reported security, the reported trade price, the price to the customer and the difference between them.'),
('A firm buys corporate bonds and sells them the same day to a retail customer as principal. Under Rule 2232 the confirmation must show the mark-up:',
 'In dollars and as a percent of prevailing market price', ["Only as a percentage of the bond's face amount", 'Only if the customer asks for it in writing', "Only on the customer's year-end statement"],
 'Rule 2232(c) requires mark-up disclosure for corporate and agency debt sold to a non-institutional customer when the firm made offsetting principal trades the same trading day, expressed as a total dollar amount and a percentage of prevailing market price.'),
('Under Rule 2232, a confirmation for a corporate bond sale to a non-institutional customer must also show:',
 'The time of execution, to the second', ["The bond's original issue price", "The issuer's credit rating history", "The firm's inventory of the bond that day"],
 "Rule 2232(c) requires confirmations of these trades to show the execution time expressed to the second, with a reference and, for electronic confirmations, a link to FINRA's TRACE data page for the security."),
('A buying firm intends to buy in securities a seller has failed to deliver. Under Rule 11810 its written buy-in notice must reach the seller by:',
 '12 noon Eastern, two business days before the buy-in', ['4 p.m. Eastern on the day of the buy-in', '12 noon Eastern, five business days before the buy-in', 'The close of business on the settlement date'],
 "Rule 11810(b)(1) requires written notice to be delivered to the seller's office not later than 12:00 noon Eastern time, two business days before execution of the proposed buy-in."),
('A firm receives a retransmitted buy-in notice from a party it owes securities to. It must pass the notice on so it reaches its own seller by:',
 '12 noon Eastern, the business day before the buy-in', ['The same time that is stated in the original notice', 'The end of the buy-in day', 'Three business days before the buy-in'],
 'Rule 11810(b)(5) requires immediate retransmittal, with the retransmitted notice delivered by 12 noon Eastern on the business day preceding the date of the proposed buy-in.'),
('A customer sells stock in a cash account but has not delivered the shares 10 business days after the settlement date. Under SEC Rule 15c3-3(m) the firm must:',
 'Close out the sale by buying in the shares', ['Extend the settlement date by 30 days', 'Cancel the sale and rebill the buyer', 'Report the customer to FINRA as a fail'],
 'Rule 15c3-3(m) requires a broker-dealer to close out a customer sell order by purchasing securities of like kind and quantity if the customer has not delivered them within 10 business days after the settlement date, unless an extension applies.'),
('In an off-exchange trade between two FINRA member firms in an equity security, the trade report is generally made by:',
 'The member on the sell side', ['The member on the buy side', 'Both members, as separate reports', 'The clearing firm of the buyer'],
 "Under FINRA's equity trade reporting rules, in a trade between two members the executing party is the sell-side member, which reports the trade; in a trade with a non-member or customer, the member reports."),
('Under FINRA Rule 6730, most corporate bond trades must be reported to TRACE as soon as practicable and no later than:',
 '15 minutes after execution', ['10 seconds after execution', '1 hour after execution', 'The end of the trading day'],
 'Rule 6730(a)(1) sets an outer limit of 15 minutes for TRACE-eligible securities such as corporate bonds. FINRA withdrew its proposal to cut that window to one minute in Regulatory Notice 25-17.'),
("Which trade is reported to FINRA's TRACE system?",
 'A corporate bond trade', ['A trade in a municipal bond', 'An exchange trade in a listed option', 'An exchange trade in a listed stock'],
 'TRACE collects transactions in TRACE-eligible securities such as corporate, agency and Treasury debt. Municipal trades go to the MSRB, and exchange trades are reported by the exchanges.'),
('A member executes a trade in an OTC equity security that is not an NMS stock. It reports the trade to:',
 'The OTC Reporting Facility', ['A FINRA Trade Reporting Facility', 'The TRACE system for debt', "The MSRB's RTRS system"],
 'Under the Rule 6600 Series, trades in OTC equity securities (non-NMS stocks) are reported to the ORF. Off-exchange trades in NMS stocks go to a Trade Reporting Facility or the Alternative Display Facility.'),
('A retail customer buys a callable bond in a trade effected on the basis of yield to call. Besides that yield, the Rule 10b-10 confirmation must show:',
 'The type of call, the call date and the call price', ["The issuer's full credit rating history", 'The names of the other buyers in the issue', "The bond's credit rating at issue"],
 'Rule 10b-10(a)(6) requires, for a debt trade effected on the basis of yield, the yield used and its type, and if effected at yield to call, the type of call, the call date and the call price, plus the dollar price.'),
('Under Rule 2231, a firm must send customers account statements at least:',
 'Once each calendar quarter', ['Once each calendar year', 'Once every six months', 'Only in months with trades'],
 'Rule 2231 requires general securities members to send account statements at least once each calendar quarter to each customer with a balance or position, showing activity and positions.'),
('An adviser places one block order for several of its managed accounts. To avoid favoring some accounts, the allocation should:',
 'Follow a fair method set before or when it is placed', ['Be decided after seeing which accounts would profit', 'Give the best fills to the largest accounts', "Be left to the trader's judgment each day"],
 'Allocating block trades after the results are known can let a firm favor some accounts. Supervisors should require a fair allocation method determined before or at the time of the order and documented.'),
('A cash account customer buys stock and fails to pay by the Regulation T deadline, and the firm sells the stock out. Unless the firm gets relief, the account is:',
 'Frozen for 90 days: cash must be in before any purchase', ['Closed permanently by the firm', 'Converted to a margin account with a call', 'Restricted only for the next trade the customer makes'],
 'Under Regulation T section 220.8, if a customer sells a security before paying for it or fails to pay, the account is frozen for 90 days, during which the customer must have cash in the account before any purchase is executed.'),
('Under SEC Rule 15c6-2, for institutional trades that need allocations, confirmations and affirmations, a broker-dealer must have agreements or policies to complete them:',
 'As soon as practicable, by the end of trade date', ['Within three business days after the trade date', 'By the end of the settlement date', "Before the customer's next quarterly statement"],
 'Rule 15c6-2, adopted with the move to T+1 settlement, requires either written agreements or policies reasonably designed to ensure completion of allocations, confirmations and affirmations as soon as technologically practicable and no later than the end of trade date.'),
]
